## [4.12.0] - 2026-08-25

### Added
- Rhythm-aware vibration engine v9.1
- Global beat gate with 195ms minimum interval
- Three-band timbre analysis (Bass/Mid/High)
- Dynamic intensity mapping based on peak follower
- Bilingual README (Chinese/English)
- NO_BUG_CHARM.webp for good luck

### Changed
- **v9.1**: Fixed peak follower to track attack delta instead of RMS level
  - KICK now has real dynamics: 255, 199, 89, 224... (was stuck at constant values)
  - Increased peak decay speed from 0.0006 to 0.005 for faster response
- **v9.0**: Complete redesign with global beat gate
  - Fast tracks (>140 BPM) automatically keep only strong beats
  - Minimum 195ms interval between vibrations
- **v8.0**: Simplified beat detection conditions
  - Reduced from 4 conditions to 2 core conditions
  - More beats are now detected correctly
- **v7.0**: Fixed HapticEngine intensity scaling
  - Changed minimum normalized value from 0.35 to 0.1
  - Allows 10%-100% dynamic range instead of 35%-100%

### Fixed
- Peak follower tracking RMS level instead of attack delta (caused constant intensity)
- HapticEngine forcing minimum 35% intensity (all vibrations felt the same)
- Beat detection conditions too strict (many beats were missed)
- BPM detection unstable (single-sample measurement)

### Technical Details

#### v9.1 Core Fix
```kotlin
// Before: Tracking RMS level (constant ~0.17)
peakLow = max(peakLow, rmsLow)
rel = rmsLow / peakLow  // Always ≈ 1.0

// After: Tracking attack delta
peakLow = max(peakLow, rmsLow) * (1 - peakDecay)
peakDelta = rmsLow - peakLow
rel = peakDelta / (peakLow + 0.01f)  // Now has real dynamics
```

